{
  "title": "PWM Motor Drive",
  "description": "A 555 in astable mode drives a MOSFET that switches a motor, with a flyback diode.",
  "education": {
    "summary": "PWM switches the load on and off quickly; the average voltage sets the speed. The flyback diode gives the motor current somewhere to go when the switch opens.",
    "objectives": [
      "Compute a 555 astable frequency",
      "Explain duty cycle",
      "Know why inductive loads need a flyback diode"
    ],
    "experiments": [
      "Change R2 and watch the duty cycle and motor speed change."
    ]
  },
